{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ורוח אלהים מרחפת", :translit "v'ruach elohim m'rachefet", :gloss "and the spirit of God hovered"} {:he "רוחו של משיח", :translit "rucho shel mashiach", :gloss "his spirit of the anointed one"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ורוח אלהים מרחפת", :b "זו רוחו של משיח"}], :frame {:text "The Targum renders 'ורוח אלהים מרחפת' as 'ורוחא מן קדם יוי מרחפא על אפי מיא' — and from before the Lord a wind was hovering over the face of the waters — which the Talmud (Chagigah 12a) identifies as the earth-spirit. Genesis Rabbah 2:4 records a dispute: one opinion identifies this spirit as the spirit of the Messiah. The Midrash Tanchuma (Bereshit 2) likewise teaches that the spirit of the Messiah hovered over the waters at creation.", :sources ["Targum Onkelos Genesis 1:2" "Chagigah 12a" "Bereshit Rabbah 2:4" "Midrash Tanchuma Bereshit 2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ורוח אלהים מרחפת", :a-value 1034, :b "זו רוחו של משיח", :b-value 921, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:03:41.075642270Z", :model "glm-5.2"}